{"title":"Logarithm","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Logarithms</b> are right inverses of powers.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Applications\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Applications</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Discrete_Logarithm\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Discrete Logarithm</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Properties\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Properties</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Natural_Logarithm\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Natural Logarithm</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problems_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Videos\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Videos</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#More\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">More</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Logarithms, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_inverse\" title=\"Right inverse\">right inverses</a> of powers can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29cbd419c9ac4dcc080d7d5b6ab5ba41b168d5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_a(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf2481826c1e451d75cffed5f8e3e2b554bec85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{\\log_a(b)}=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Applications\">Applications</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Applications\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Some of the real powerful uses of logarithms come down to never having to deal with massive numbers. For example,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d71de6de6879b85ba87043005113b6efd5b42b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[((((((3^5)^6)^7)^8)^9)^{10})^{11}=\\underbrace{1177\\ldots 1}_{\\text{793549 digits}}\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"39\" /> would be a pain to have to calculate any time you wanted to use it (say in a comparison of large numbers). Its natural logarithm though (partly due to \nleft to right parenthesized exponentiation) is only 7 digits before the decimal point. Comparing the logs of the numbers to a given precision can allow easier comparison than computing and comparing the numbers themselves. Logs also allow (with repetition) to turn left to right exponentiation into power towers (especially useful for tetration (exponentiation repetition with the same exponent)). For example,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/80189d6c36917f8c1176fafd9ce09d960a2096af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_4(3)\\approx 0.7924812503605780907268694720\\ldots\\]\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/8631a97953e0a3cb66d72b3fb9d0f44dca8c8a12.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_4(5)\\approx 1.160964047443681173935159715\\ldots\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242b4dd3cb976c28d76e85920dd77e9d1226d757.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_4(6)\\approx 1.292481250360578090726869472\\ldots\\]\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b22c0d80cf13f58506aa150351b186c4ee458c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_4(\\log_4(3))\\approx -0.1677756462730553083259853611\\ldots\\]\" width=\"428\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Therefore by: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63eacce0ec0821ad9fe0e08e4cfc09125ba13fb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{(a^b)}^c=a^{bc}\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"21\" /> and identities 1 and 2 above (2 being used twice), we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d65c3cb22faee07180edae32423df99740ab802.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_4(\\log_4(3))+(\\log_4(5)+\\log_4(6))\\approx 2.285669651531203956336043826\\ldots=x\\]\" width=\"592\" height=\"18\" /> such that:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e49543b1f4b86a8e9386b5c4d55f12a14f7744af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(^24)^x=4^{4^x}\\approx(3^5)^6\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Discrete_Logarithm\">Discrete Logarithm</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Discrete Logarithm\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>An only partially related value is the discrete logarithm, used in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cryptography\" title=\"Cryptography\">cryptography</a> via <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_arithmetic\" title=\"Modular arithmetic\">modular arithmetic</a>. It's the lowest value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/35611762e683fed8fc47f1338ee8b0cad3434abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^c=mx+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" /> for given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe022969b65e0bee035c1b856dce00bcdaa8f0c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,m,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> being integers (as well as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d7e08303b6710aad476fcf9df46fff54f6fc278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"11\" /> the unknowns being integers). \n</p><p>It's related to the usual logarithm by the fact that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> isn't an integer power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e392ba75388d0fa2703559bb676838477a8677e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil \\log_a(m)\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"19\" /> is a lower bound on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm_Properties\" title=\"Logarithm Properties\">Logarithm Properties</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li>Evaluate:</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cca2f4656391b617fda7e10267bdde741d7a27b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\log_{50}{2.5})(\\log_{2.5}e)(\\ln{2500})\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<ol><li>Evaluate:</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/6/8b63a7a03f77bbf6da61a45c90734ed1c7ddba2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\log_2 3)(\\log_3 4)(\\log_4 5) \\cdots (\\log_{2005} 2006)\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<ol><li>Simplify the following expression:</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9a5834ee1ae2b56b880bf3bbbb708504c333a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{\\log_2 N} + \\frac{1}{\\log_3 N} + \\frac{1}{\\log_4 N} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{\\log_{100} N},\\]\" width=\"343\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>where \\( N = (100!)^3 \\).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Natural_Logarithm\">Natural Logarithm</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Natural Logarithm\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <b>natural logarithm</b> is the logarithm with base <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=E\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"E\">e</a>.  It is usually denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30d938049e2d8bdbff5c53527041fc1dac96cb49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />, an abbreviation of the French <i>logarithme normal</i>, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/086a1575ba540770e6e85a7d4c467496e9957cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln(x) = \\log_e(x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />  However, in higher mathematics such as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_analysis\" title=\"Complex analysis\">complex analysis</a>, the base 10 logarithm is typically disposed with entirely, the symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/8/698c1c9cde3469a346091405ffbbcedf96609562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"16\" /> is taken to mean the logarithm base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and the symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30d938049e2d8bdbff5c53527041fc1dac96cb49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> is not used at all.  (This is an example of conflicting <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_convention\" title=\"Mathematical convention\">mathematical conventions</a>.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e8987dc61784d3592070940ac9fce0d4b33cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln a$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> can also be defined as the area under the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a146369c3dd83adc390b3aa92292b7b09bd2b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> between 1 and a, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d2230cca528436a43afdf0085232ae3df010bcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int^a_1 \\frac{1}{x}\\, dx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"65\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>All logarithms are undefined in nonpositive reals, as they are complex. From the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/156034947c1c1c310bc5c19bc1b9b8f772d3539d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{i\\pi}=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd4ada75cfdf1433987d69b7a97a5cf4da3d4ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln (-1)=i\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. Additionally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc8019d2830a3eb3ef849fd93e2bd6f68ebeae78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln (-n)=\\ln n+i\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> for positive real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems_2\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b685bdf777d825df5061a0d16397af70dbb8127.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1{\\log_2a}+\\frac1{\\log_3a}+\\frac1{\\log_4a}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"219\" height=\"41\" />?</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\"> Source</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>Positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> satisfy the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d802124c062e56f7fd4b870e1f445d902ed9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2(\\log_{2^a}(\\log_{2^b}(2^{1000})))=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"19\" /> Find the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Source</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56551a1cd4be3a5d996736e858917416035f3c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_sequence\" title=\"Geometric sequence\">geometric</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/58488fe7417bd8f77addd0093869b2f34bce7896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" /> and common <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e1630c915bd1b27bfa1f505bf1ac0bb9f5d61f32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e7622b770463e363f03953bcdfe6dc6e0d42f50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_8 a_1+\\log_8 a_2+\\cdots+\\log_8 a_{12} = 2006,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"17\" /> find the number of possible ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52f317d8803bc8311c580ef9a88d6dcdd805906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,r).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /></li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">Source</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li>The solutions to the system of equations</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59e46a564aaaca905d62986e77523e98fa0618a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{225}x+\\log_{64}y=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/1226b24f95e00e2b64504c177aa2b07818ebbd75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{x}225-\\log_{y}64=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"169\" height=\"19\" />\nare <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b354638f824de285dce6d6d3f72163cb287aeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/871e8d2e83189f86381352faa5c18c2d0cf3f3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_2,y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b374a7b04c4848a628d98ccb1de4ed43fc5fa7a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{30}\\left(x_1y_1x_2y_2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Source</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Videos\">Videos</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Videos\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/CxXc_moY-3Q\">Five-minute Intro to Logarithms</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/fU7B2H4JJCU\">Introduction to Logarithms</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//youtu.be/tUUynpSD5DM\">Logarithms Properties</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z5myJ8dg_rM\">Khan Academy</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.youtube.com/watch?v=ey7ttABX9SM\">Two-minute Intro to Logarithms</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"More\">More</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: More\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm_Properties\" title=\"Logarithm Properties\">Logarithm Properties</a>\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018000858\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 320/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9811/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.438      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.438      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1943:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018000858 and revision id 273208. Rendering was tri